.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt VITRINE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vitrine
.Nd HTML artifacts that transclude markdown sections
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds and serves HTML artifacts whose
.Ql md-section
elements transclude sections of markdown documents.
The markdown stays the single source; the artifact renders it.
A baked copy works as a plain file, and the server upgrades it to a
live render with a response inbox.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "extract <file>"
.It Cm new Ar slug
Scaffold an artifact directory with the runtime under
.Pa .vitrine/<slug>/ .
.It Cm sync Op Ar slug
Bake each
.Ql md-section
element from its source.
Without
.Ar slug ,
sync every artifact.
.It Cm serve Op Fl -port Ar n
Serve the artifacts and the response inbox on 127.0.0.1.
Only
.Pa .vitrine/
content and markdown files are served.
A POST to
.Pa /respond/<slug>
lands in the artifact's
.Pa responses/
directory and
.Pa latest.json .
.It Cm resolve Ar ref
Resolve a
.Ql tisket: ,
.Ql zettel: ,
or
.Ql file:
ref, with an optional
.Ql #anchor ,
to its source file.
.It Cm extract Ar file Op Ar anchor
List the anchors in a markdown file, or print one section.
.It Cm render Ar file
Render a markdown file to HTML on stdout.
.It Cm docs Op Ar page
Print the bundled documentation.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tisket 1 ,
.Xr zettel 1
